    "body": "Hey!\r\n\r\nFirst of all - Awesome work on this project! We've begun using it for transparency and had great feedback, so I'd like to pass that straight back to you guys who did the hard work.\r\n\r\nI know this could be a point of contention due to the risk of abuse, but I'd really like to be able to set up a subscription where a user cannot unsubscribe, and ideally, doesn't need confirmation (The latter I can kinda work around). This is because we're looking to automatically send updates to staff and students for any issues, and currently any person who is a member of these global mailing lists can remove the entire group!\r\n\r\nCurrently we're duplicating the effort by sending an issue with a manual link to any incidents, but we'd much rather it run from one place - Plus the CachetHQ emails are very pretty.\r\n\r\nNow, I'm aware that this could be abused in some scenarios, so I'm not sure how this could be implemented in a way that satisfies both sides?\r\n\r\nCheers,\r\nJames.\r\n",
